        "client_msg_id": "4aa2b539-e12a-4e0c-8ea8-ef261835e61c",
        "text": "I find it a bit counterintuitive that `%in%` performs worse than `any(x == )` for character strings. Am I missing something :thinking_face: ?\n```x <- sample(letters, 1e3, replace = TRUE)\n\nmicrobenchmark::microbenchmark(\"a\" %in% x, any(\"a\" == x), times = 1e5)\n#> Unit: microseconds\n#>           expr   min    lq     mean median    uq      max neval\n#>     \"a\" %in% x 1.634 3.482 4.229705  3.792 4.155 3235.933 1e+05\n#>  any(\"a\" == x) 1.464 2.305 2.681631  2.487 2.701 3977.443 1e+05\n\nx <- sample(1:1e6, 1e3, replace = TRUE)\n\nmicrobenchmark::microbenchmark(1L %in% x, any(1L == x), times = 1e5)\n#> Unit: nanoseconds\n#>          expr  min   lq      mean median   uq     max neval\n#>     1L %in% x  487  663  895.5988    727  818 1695764 1e+05\n#>  any(1L == x) 1077 1127 1307.8984   1174 1271 1553942 1e+05```",
        "team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "user_team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "source_team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
