        "text": "In other words, I would expect `%in%` to perform dramatically better here. But you are right that since it uses `match()`, it doesn't work this way...\n```x &lt;- sample(letters, 1e3, replace = TRUE)\n\nmicrobenchmark::microbenchmark(\"a\" %in% c(\"a\", x), any(\"a\" == c(\"a\", x)), times = 1e5, check = \"identical\")\n#&gt; Unit: microseconds\n#&gt;                   expr   min    lq     mean median    uq      max neval\n#&gt;     \"a\" %in% c(\"a\", x) 5.382 6.174 8.178269  6.613 7.158 4375.525 1e+05\n#&gt;  any(\"a\" == c(\"a\", x)) 5.138 5.732 6.993823  6.019 6.416 4495.240 1e+05```",
